# Build context for the Dockerfile (PRD M10-T1). Keep it to what the image
# needs: requirements.txt, src/, config/ and the web/ sources. Everything else is
# either personal (data/, archive/ - the repo is public, the image may be too),
# host-built (node_modules), or noise.

# --- personal / state: never baked into an image ---------------------------
data/
archive/
output/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.env
.env.*

# --- the SPA is rebuilt inside the image by the node stage -----------------
# Excluding the committed bundle proves the image serves what the node stage
# built, not a possibly stale copy from the checkout.
src/jobscraper/web/static/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.vite/
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# --- repo / tooling --------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
docs/
tests/
scripts/
README.md
run.ps1
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore

# --- caches ----------------------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
build/
dist/

# --- os / editor / worktree junk -------------------------------------------
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.orig
*.rej
